{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310822,"nonce":"dURnmoh1yC7uxrv5+8FziSEtWHk=","title":"rayzor_tensor_add_into landed — F32 NEON/SSE2 in-place fused add eliminates the alloc+memcpy+free per residual / FFN-up / bias add. Bench ...","message":"In-place fused add primitive (`Tensor.addInto`) landed at commits 550c208 + a98a3a8 + da4614c. Replaces the alloc+memcpy+free per residual / FFN-up / bias add in the transformer hot loop. Saves ~3 `[seq, hidden]` F32 allocs per layer per token; matmul still ~95% CPU so wall-clock gains are minimal at 24-token decode (Llama 3.2 1B).\n\n**Why landed despite small bench win:** the architecture hygiene matters more than the immediate speedup. addInto removes per-step new-tensor alloc, which composes with the pool allocator (next workflow) — together they're the foundation for shape-class arena reuse (KV-cache growth, attention scratch). Strict `@:move` enforcement ([[project-move-clone-enforced]]) and Tier B clone semantics make the safety story hold.\n\n**How to apply:** when proposing optimisations on the residual / accumulator path, prefer `dst.addInto(src)` over `var y = dst.add(src)`. Dest must be contiguous (asserted by the runtime kernel; abort with diagnostic if violated). Receiver must be a fresh-or-last-use binding — `@:move` enforces this at compile time on `@:move`-annotated classes.\n\n\n`rayzor_tensor_add_into(dest, src) -\u003e ()` at [runtime/src/tensor.rs:1381](runtime/src/tensor.rs#L1381). Safety contract (every violation aborts with eprintln diagnostic):\n\n- Non-null pointers\n- Identical ndim / shape / numel / dtype\n- Dest contiguous (`RayzorTensor::is_contiguous` walks strides numpy-style; length-1 axes ignored)\n- `dest.data != src.data` (pointer-equality alias guard)\n\nFast path: `tensor_simd::add_assign_slice` — NEON `vaddq_f32` / SSE2 `_mm_add_ps` over 4-lane chunks + scalar tail. Single `\u0026mut [f32]` + `\u0026[f32]` signature; SIMD intrinsics operate on raw pointers from `dst.as_mut_ptr()`. The prior `\u0026mut [f32]` / `\u0026[f32]` aliased pair was Rust aliasing-model UB regardless of load-before-store ordering — caught by the wqeyqlth8 adversarial reviewers; fixed before commit.\n\nStrided-src gather path: walks dest's contiguous counter, recomputes multi-index, applies src.strides. F16 / BF16 scalar fallback with eprintln warning.\n\nABI: returns `()`, matching the Tensor.hx surface and the stdlib extern decl. Original Rust signature returned `i64` (the dest pointer) — harmless on ARM64/x86_64 but a WASM lowering tripwire; reconciled before commit.\n\n\nThree-layer: extern decl in `compiler/src/stdlib/tensor.rs`, instance mapping `rayzor_ds_Tensor.addInto -\u003e Tensor_addInto` in `compiler/src/stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs`, Haxe surface `public function addInto(src: Tensor): Void` in `compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/ds/Tensor.hx`.\n\n\nFour rewrites land:\n- [TransformerBlock.hx:54](nue/nue/transformer/TransformerBlock.hx#L54) pre-norm residual\n- [TransformerBlock.hx:59](nue/nue/transformer/TransformerBlock.hx#L59) post-FFN residual\n- [LayerNorm.hx:33](nue/nue/transformer/LayerNorm.hx#L33) bias add (cold for Llama; warm for GPT-2/BERT)\n- [Linear.hx:86](nue/nue/Linear.hx#L86) bias add (cold for Llama; warm for Qwen2/encoders)\n\nAll four dests verified fresh contiguous owning allocations; no permuted-view route reaches the kernel. src side is fresh or read-only model parameter.\n\n\nM1 Pro / Llama 3.2 1B Instruct Q4_K_M / 24 tokens / 3 runs, **same-session A/B** (rewrites stashed vs applied, runtime addInto + stdlib binding present in both):\n\n- Wall: 14.23 s → 14.34 s = **+0.8%**\n- tok/s: 0.853 → 0.854 = **~0%**\n\nInside the documented ~16% run-to-run noise band. The audit's `\u003c=1-2%` prediction holds.\n\n**Misattribution risk** flagged by the workflow synthesis: the regression-section's \"27% wall favorable\" delta compared current HEAD to the audit's 20.15 s baseline, which spans multiple intervening qmatmul SIMD commits (7187129, c55255e, 7423e04, afd3018). NOT attributable to addInto. Commit messages anchor to the honest same-session A/B.\n\n**Memory churn**: 3 saved `[seq, hidden=2048]` F32 allocs / layer / token = ~384 KB/token; ~9 MB allocator churn over a 24-token bench. Peak RSS impact below sampling noise on a 2.4 GB model. **Prefill-heavy / longer-context runs should show larger wins** (per-token alloc grows linearly with seq); 8B-class models (hidden=8192) scale 4x.\n\n\n1. **Range-overlap alias guard**: current `d.data == s.data` only catches identical pointers; a sub-view producer with offset would slip past. No such producer exists today but watch when slicing/view APIs grow.\n2. **Negative tests for abort paths**: alias-abort, non-contiguous dest, dtype/shape/ndim mismatch are currently uncovered. Convert `abort()` to `panic!` in a debug-build cfg to enable `#[should_panic]` coverage.\n3. **Strided-src gather CI test**: the slow path has no CI invocation today. Construct a permuted-view source in a unit test (~25 LOC) to lock in correctness.\n4. **Hoist `d_shape[k+1..].iter().product()` out of the inner loop** in the strided gather path — currently O(numel · ndim²).\n5. **F16 / BF16 vectorised path**: scalar fallback today; NEON has native f16 ops via `vcvt`.\n6. **[[bugs-addinto-rebind-clone-drop-failure]]** — LlamaModel.hx:65 defensive clone cannot be dropped; the bare `h = block.forward(h)` rebinding SIGSEGVs. This was the audit's headline ~3 MB allocator-churn win; the remaining clone makes the rewrite mostly architecture-hygiene at present. Root-cause is the drop analyzer / IR scope cleanup, not addInto itself.\n7. **@:move asymmetry**: Haxe has no `\u0026mut`/borrow concept; the analyzer treats `x.addInto(other)` as a method-call read of x. Future direction: model addInto as `mut self` so the type system rejects aliased reads after the call, not just at clone-introduction time.\n\n\n- [[project-move-clone-enforced]] — `@:move` runtime-load-bearing makes alias-aware optimisations safe\n- Pool allocator (next workflow) — shape-class arena reuse removes the per-step alloc churn that addInto only reduces\n- Future: addInto fastpath that takes `Tensor` as both args via a `borrow_mut` token, eliminating the runtime alias check\n\n\n`wqeyqlth8` — 9 agents, 639k tokens. Three-perspective adversarial verify (correctness / regression / aliasing) all flagged the same two latent defects (aliasing UB + ABI mismatch); both fixed before commit.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_addinto_fused_kernel` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}